      "id": 27,
      "title": "New Research Reveals Autistic Brains Process Faces Differently",
      "url": "https://scitechdaily.com/new-research-reveals-autistic-brains-process-faces-differently/",
      "summary": "Autistic children showed earlier and less age-related refinement in the brain signals involved in processing faces. A child looks at a face, and within milliseconds the brain begins sorting its features, expression, and identity. Researchers have now traced that process across the entire scalp in one of the most comprehensive studies of face perception in [...]",
